Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	Read regressions remain explicit costs of the lifetime/ownership design. Ordinary Direct allocation is 10,112 / 10,264 / 10,248 bytes per operation (dev/parent/final), so allocation volume alone does not explain the cost. Attach benefits from #132’s pooled host against dev but still pays #133’s independent close machinery against its parent. Prior isolated guard/thread experiments and profiling are retained in the historical options report below; this PR adds no broader counter/guard/inline-close optimization. Performance acceptance is separate from the safety gate. All **84 comparison processes and 420 measured windows** are retained and verified; an immutable archive link follows after hosted validation completes.
