Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	### Public surface and compatibility
Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	
Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	
Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	- Typed/BSON collections, queries, Include, vector queries, indexes and metadata are bound. Read-only Direct and Shared handles query and complete without granting writes.
Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	- SQL, FileStorage and maintenance are not exposed on handles. Collection drop/rename and external/system query I/O reject before mutation; metadata `$cols`/`$indexes` is supported.
Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	- Coordinated/custom/decorated engines inside `LiteDatabase`, Shared private memory/temp storage, and Shared caller data/log/temp streams reject handles. Direct caller streams remain supported. Ordinary/legacy provider support is unchanged.
Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	- Existing `ILiteDatabase`/`ILiteEngine` implementers gain no required members. Concrete `BeginTransaction` plus optional provider/extension supplies the new capability.
Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	- Legacy transaction signatures and valid synchronous behavior remain; CS0618 deprecates them with a warning. Warnings-as-errors projects can migrate with the documented targeted exception.
Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	- Outcomes distinguish Committed, RolledBack, Failed and Indeterminate. Known committed outcomes survive cleanup failures; failed durable flushes never become a successful rollback. Original errors retain secondary cleanup diagnostics. Closed facade access rejects with `ObjectDisposedException`.
Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	- Native admission, MMFs/sidecars, filesystem support, isolation, file formats and configured durability remain inherited from #132. Parameterless Shared begin keeps unbounded waiting; the new opt-in overload bounds both local/native writer waits and supports begin-only cancellation. Collection TIMEOUT remains separate.
